{
  "id": "01-the-old-life",
  "title": "Lay Down the Old Life",
  "tenet": "Let the flesh lose its rule",
  "durationMs": 67128,
  "audioAsset": "kingdom/01-the-old-life.mp3",
  "transcriptAsset": "assets/kingdom/01-the-old-life.json",
  "text": "What keeps choosing for you when you mean to choose Christ?\n\nA boy watched his father repair the gate beside their small garden. Each morning it stood open again, and hungry animals wandered through the seedlings. The boy wanted to chase the animals farther away. His father showed him the bent latch. Together they straightened it and fastened the gate. The next morning the boy checked it himself. Soon checking the gate became part of caring for the garden.\n\nThe flesh is like that old rule within us: the reflex to grasp, hide, retaliate, or take the easier pleasure. The body is not our enemy, and a person is never a ruined garden. But an impulse becomes a master when we obey it without asking where it leads. Jesus invites us to bring that impulse into the light, receive mercy, and learn a different response. Grace does not leave us standing outside the gate. It gives us strength to take hold of the latch. What desire has been deciding for you lately? Name it honestly in prayer. Then choose one small act of self control today. Check the gate again tomorrow.",
